@anon.b4276b7b39cc559116fc5d29527aa342.1923 = private unnamed_addr constant [1962 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for the use of boolean positional arguments in function definitions,\0Aas determined by the presence of a boolean default value.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0ACalling a function with boolean positional arguments is confusing as the\0Ameaning of the boolean value is not clear to the caller and to future\0Areaders of the code.\0A\0AThe use of a boolean will also limit the function to only two possible\0Abehaviors, which makes the function difficult to extend in the future.\0A\0AInstead, consider refactoring into separate implementations for the\0A`True` and `False` cases, using an `Enum`, or making the argument a\0Akeyword-only argument, to force callers to be explicit when providing\0Athe argument.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Afrom math import ceil, floor\0A\0A\0Adef round_number(number, up=True):\0A    return ceil(number) if up else floor(number)\0A\0A\0Around_number(1.5, True)  # What does `True` mean?\0Around_number(1.5, False)  # What does `False` mean?\0A```\0A\0AInstead, refactor into separate implementations:\0A```python\0Afrom math import ceil, floor\0A\0A\0Adef round_up(number):\0A    return ceil(number)\0A\0A\0Adef round_down(number):\0A    return floor(number)\0A\0A\0Around_up(1.5)\0Around_down(1.5)\0A```\0A\0AOr, refactor to use an `Enum`:\0A```python\0Afrom enum import Enum\0A\0A\0Aclass RoundingMethod(Enum):\0A    UP = 1\0A    DOWN = 2\0A\0A\0Adef round_number(value, method):\0A    return ceil(number) if method is RoundingMethod.UP else floor(number)\0A\0A\0Around_number(1.5, RoundingMethod.UP)\0Around_number(1.5, RoundingMethod.DOWN)\0A```\0A\0AOr, make the argument a keyword-only argument:\0A```python\0Afrom math import ceil, floor\0A\0A\0Adef round_number(number, *, up=True):\0A    return ceil(number) if up else floor(number)\0A\0A\0Around_number(1.5, up=True)\0Around_number(1.5, up=False)\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: Calls](https://docs.python.org/3/reference/expressions.html#calls)\0A- [_How to Avoid \E2\80\9CThe Boolean Trap\E2\80\9D_ by Adam Johnson](https://adamj.eu/tech/2021/07/10/python-type-hints-how-to-avoid-the-boolean-trap/)\0A", align 1
