@anon.b4276b7b39cc559116fc5d29527aa342.2032 = private unnamed_addr constant [448 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for functions in stub (`.pyi`) files that contain multiple\0Astatements.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AStub files are never executed, and are only intended to define type hints.\0AAs such, functions in stub files should not contain functional code, and\0Ashould instead contain only a single statement (e.g., `...`).\0A\0A## Example\0A\0A```pyi\0Adef function():\0A    x = 1\0A    y = 2\0A    return x + y\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A\0A```pyi\0Adef function(): ...\0A```\0A", align 1
