@anon.b4276b7b39cc559116fc5d29527aa342.2052 = private unnamed_addr constant [833 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for uses of exception-related assertion methods from the `unittest`\0Amodule.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0ATo enforce the assertion style recommended by `pytest`, `pytest.raises` is\0Apreferred over the exception-related assertion methods in `unittest`, like\0A`assertRaises`.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aimport unittest\0A\0A\0Aclass TestFoo(unittest.TestCase):\0A    def test_foo(self):\0A        with self.assertRaises(ValueError):\0A            raise ValueError(\22foo\22)\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aimport unittest\0Aimport pytest\0A\0A\0Aclass TestFoo(unittest.TestCase):\0A    def test_foo(self):\0A        with pytest.raises(ValueError):\0A            raise ValueError(\22foo\22)\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [`pytest` documentation: Assertions about expected exceptions](https://docs.pytest.org/en/latest/how-to/assert.html#assertions-about-expected-exceptions)\0A", align 1
