@anon.b4276b7b39cc559116fc5d29527aa342.2057 = private unnamed_addr constant [887 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for argument-free `@pytest.fixture()` decorators with or without\0Aparentheses, depending on the [`lint.flake8-pytest-style.fixture-parentheses`]\0Asetting.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AIf a `@pytest.fixture()` doesn't take any arguments, the parentheses are\0Aoptional.\0A\0AEither removing those unnecessary parentheses _or_ requiring them for all\0Afixtures is fine, but it's best to be consistent. The rule defaults to\0Aremoving unnecessary parentheses, to match the documentation of the\0Aofficial pytest projects.\0A\0A## Example\0A\0A```python\0Aimport pytest\0A\0A\0A@pytest.fixture()\0Adef my_fixture(): ...\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A\0A```python\0Aimport pytest\0A\0A\0A@pytest.fixture\0Adef my_fixture(): ...\0A```\0A\0A## Options\0A- `lint.flake8-pytest-style.fixture-parentheses`\0A\0A## References\0A- [`pytest` documentation: API Reference: Fixtures](https://docs.pytest.org/en/latest/reference/reference.html#fixtures-api)\0A", align 1
