@anon.b4276b7b39cc559116fc5d29527aa342.2156 = private unnamed_addr constant [653 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for nested `if` statements that can be collapsed into a single `if`\0Astatement.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0ANesting `if` statements leads to deeper indentation and makes code harder to\0Aread. Instead, combine the conditions into a single `if` statement with an\0A`and` operator.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aif foo:\0A    if bar:\0A        ...\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aif foo and bar:\0A    ...\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: The `if` statement](https://docs.python.org/3/reference/compound_stmts.html#the-if-statement)\0A- [Python documentation: Boolean operations](https://docs.python.org/3/reference/expressions.html#boolean-operations)\0A", align 1
