@anon.b4276b7b39cc559116fc5d29527aa342.2166 = private unnamed_addr constant [758 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for `inplace=True` usages in `pandas` function and method\0Acalls.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AUsing `inplace=True` encourages mutation rather than immutable data,\0Awhich is harder to reason about and may cause bugs. It also removes the\0Aability to use the method chaining style for `pandas` operations.\0A\0AFurther, in many cases, `inplace=True` does not provide a performance\0Abenefit, as `pandas` will often copy `DataFrames` in the background.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Adf.sort_values(\22col1\22, inplace=True)\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Asorted_df = df.sort_values(\22col1\22)\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [_Why You Should Probably Never Use pandas `inplace=True`_](https://towardsdatascience.com/why-you-should-probably-never-use-pandas-inplace-true-9f9f211849e4)\0A", align 1
