@anon.b4276b7b39cc559116fc5d29527aa342.2175 = private unnamed_addr constant [945 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for argument names that do not follow the `snake_case` convention.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0A[PEP 8] recommends that function names should be lower case and separated\0Aby underscores (also known as `snake_case`).\0A\0A> Function names should be lowercase, with words separated by underscores\0A> as necessary to improve readability.\0A>\0A> Variable names follow the same convention as function names.\0A>\0A> mixedCase is allowed only in contexts where that\E2\80\99s already the\0A> prevailing style (e.g. threading.py), to retain backwards compatibility.\0A\0AMethods decorated with `@typing.override` are ignored.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Adef my_function(A, myArg):\0A    pass\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Adef my_function(a, my_arg):\0A    pass\0A```\0A\0A## Options\0A- `lint.pep8-naming.ignore-names`\0A- `lint.pep8-naming.extend-ignore-names`\0A\0A[PEP 8]: https://peps.python.org/pep-0008/#function-and-method-arguments\0A[preview]: https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/preview/\0A", align 1
