@anon.b4276b7b39cc559116fc5d29527aa342.2247 = private unnamed_addr constant [523 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for imports of the `mock` module that should be replaced with\0A`unittest.mock`.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0ASince Python 3.3, `mock` has been a part of the standard library as\0A`unittest.mock`. The `mock` package is deprecated; use `unittest.mock`\0Ainstead.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aimport mock\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Afrom unittest import mock\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: `unittest.mock`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/unittest.mock.html)\0A- [PyPI: `mock`](https://pypi.org/project/mock/)\0A", align 1
