@anon.b4276b7b39cc559116fc5d29527aa342.2256 = private unnamed_addr constant [605 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for unbounded slice expressions to copy a list.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AThe `list.copy` method is more readable and consistent with copying other\0Atypes.\0A\0A## Known problems\0AThis rule is prone to false negatives due to type inference limitations,\0Aas it will only detect lists that are instantiated as literals or annotated\0Awith a type annotation.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aa = [1, 2, 3]\0Ab = a[:]\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aa = [1, 2, 3]\0Ab = a.copy()\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: Mutable Sequence Types](https://docs.python.org/3/library/stdtypes.html#mutable-sequence-types)\0A", align 1
