@anon.b4276b7b39cc559116fc5d29527aa342.2265 = private unnamed_addr constant [597 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for type checks that do not raise `TypeError`.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AThe Python documentation states that `TypeError` should be raised upon\0Aencountering an inappropriate type.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Adef foo(n: int):\0A    if isinstance(n, int):\0A        pass\0A    else:\0A        raise ValueError(\22n must be an integer\22)\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Adef foo(n: int):\0A    if isinstance(n, int):\0A        pass\0A    else:\0A        raise TypeError(\22n must be an integer\22)\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: `TypeError`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/exceptions.html#TypeError)\0A", align 1
